[META]
framework: claude-framework
file_id: CODE_CONVENTIONS
class: custom
version: 1.0.0

[CODE_CONVENTIONS]
overview: Naming, style, and architectural patterns in OpenGL Engine

[NAMESPACE_ABBREVIATIONS]
Two to four letter abbreviations for all namespaces:
  - ds: data structures (containers, allocators, storage)
  - ecs: entity-component-system framework
  - scn: scene management (hierarchy, transforms, objects)
  - gui: GUI and UI (menus, dialogs, etc.)
  - rnd: rendering and graphics pipeline
  - res: resource system (loading, caching, tags)
  - inp: input handling (keyboard, mouse, gamepad)
  - edt: editor application (panels, gizmos, tools)
  - gs: game systems (gameplay-specific)
  - cfg: configuration system
  - wnd: window and platform layer
  - app: application lifecycle and modules

[FILE_NAMING]
format: prefix_name.hpp / prefix_name.cpp
where_prefix_is: namespace abbreviation (2-4 chars)
examples:
  ✅ ds_store.hpp, ds_fixed_vector.hpp
  ✅ scn_context_set.cpp, scn_world.h
  ✅ ecs_world.hpp, ecs_system.cpp
  ❌ Store.hpp, renderer.cpp (no prefix)
  ❌ datastructures.hpp (too long prefix)

[NAMING_CONVENTIONS]
variables: snake_case (my_variable, frame_count)
functions: snake_case (get_position(), update_transform())
classes: snake_case (rare, prefer structs for data)
constants: UPPER_CASE or snake_case (depends on scope)
private_members: snake_case with m_ prefix (m_position, m_worlds)
enums: ENUM_VALUE (UPPER_CASE for options)
template_params: T, U, or CamelCase (Allocator, Traits)

[COMPONENT_NAMING]
pattern: name_component or just name (if self-descriptive)
examples:
  struct transform_component { ... } ✅
  struct position { ... } ✅ (if name is obvious)
  struct RenderData { ... } ❌ (wrong case)

[SYSTEM_NAMING]
pattern: system class inherits ecs::system_interface
files: verb_noun_system.cpp
examples:
  struct render_system : ecs::system_interface { ... }
  struct animation_system : ecs::system_interface { ... }

[INCLUDE_ORDER]
1. Module header (e.g., <snk/scene/level/scn_context_set.h>)
2. Standard library headers (cmath, vector, etc.)
3. Third-party headers (glm, boost, entt)
4. Other project headers (from other modules)

Example:
  #include <snk/scene/level/scn_context_set.h>
  #include <cmath>
  #include <glm/glm.hpp>
  #include <snk/resource/res_system.h>

[HEADER_LAYOUT]
public: <component>/include/snk/<component>/*.h, included as <snk/<component>/x.h> (angle brackets)
internal: next to the .cpp in <component>/, never installed with the SDK, included with quotes
rule: a public header must not include an internal one (glad, GLFW, assimp, impl_*, rnd_gl_*, passes/)
check: python3 tools/header_split/split.py check; CI job "SDK package" compiles every installed header

[HEADER_GUARDS]
use: #pragma once (no macro guards)
reason: Cleaner, more reliable with modern C++

[BRACES]
functions: new line
  void my_function()
  {
    // body
  }

control_flow: same line
  if (condition) {
    // body
  }
  for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    // body
  }

[COMMENTS]
language: English
style: // for single line, /* */ for blocks
when: Explain WHY, not WHAT (code shows what)
examples:
  ✅ // Cache weak_ptr because we don't own the object
  ❌ // Set flag to true

[MACROS]
naming: UPPER_CASE
scope: Minimize. Prefer constexpr functions.
namespace: Prefix with MODULE_ (e.g., ECS_ASSERT, RND_MAX_LIGHTS)
examples:
  #define ECS_MAX_WORLDS 8
  #define ASSERT_MSG(cond, msg) ...

[LOGGING_PATTERN]
never: std::cout, std::cerr, std::cin, printf
always: #include <snk/common/logger/engine_log.h> and use egLOG_* macros (spdlog backend)
note: first arg is a category string (becomes the spdlog logger name), then format args
examples:
  egLOG("resource", "Loading model: {}", path);   // egLOG == egLOG_INFO
  egLOG_WARN("resource", "Resource not found: {}", tag);
  egLOG_ERROR("render", "Failed to compile shader");
levels: egLOG_TRACE, egLOG_DEBUG, egLOG_INFO, egLOG_WARN, egLOG_ERROR

[ALLOCATOR_PATTERNS]
frame_temporaries:
  std::pmr::vector<T> vec(ds::frame_allocator());
  vec.reserve(count); // avoid realloc

persistent_data:
  std::make_shared<T>() // or use pool_resource

custom_scoped:
  ds::linear_resource scratch(size);
  std::pmr::vector<T> vec(&scratch);

[CONTAINER_PATTERNS]
performance_critical: ds::fixed_vector<T, MaxSize>
  - O(1) alloc/dealloc
  - No heap allocation
  - Use when max size is known

general_use: std::vector<T>, std::pmr::vector<T>
  - Standard vector
  - PMR vector for custom allocators (frame alloc, pool, etc.)

[SMART_POINTER_PATTERNS]
ownership: std::shared_ptr<T> or std::make_shared<T>()
non_ownership: std::weak_ptr<T> (for cycles, caches)
never: std::auto_ptr (deprecated), raw new/delete in code (use RAII)

[DESCRIPTOR_PATTERNS]
files: snake_case.desc (e.g., backpack.desc, level.desc)
format: JSON with inheritance (extends: "parent.desc")
loading: resources.require<descriptor_type>(res::tag{"res://path"})  // res::resource_system& injected; there is no global get_system()
hot_reload: Editor changes desc → binding updates entities

[RESOURCE_PATTERNS]
identification: res::tag{"res://path/to/resource"} (single-arg parses protocol)
loading: res_handle<T> h = resources.require<T>(tag); // resources: injected res::resource_system&; require_sync<T> blocks; get_system() legacy, no new uses
async: h.then([](auto& res) { /* callback; check res.has_error() */ })
cache: automatic (weak refs for auto-unload, pinned for persistent)

[ERROR_HANDLING]
assertions: ASSERT_MSG(cond, "message") from <snk/common/engine_assert.h> (active in _DEBUG only)
logging: Use egLOG_ERROR / egLOG_WARN (category-first) from engine_log.h
exceptions: Avoid in hot paths, use for init errors only
return_codes: Prefer for resource loading failures

[ECS_PATTERNS]
system_registration: ecs::system_factory::register_system<&fn>(name, { .phase, .after, .before, .run_in_edit }) — stateful: <&T::fn, T>(name, desc, ctor args...) or <&T::fn>(name, desc, shared_ptr<T>)
system_interface: empty base (virtual dtor only) — NO update()/initialize() methods
system_logic: free/member fn; args (entt::view, ctx resources) auto-injected by ecs::invoker
system_order: explicit — phase (input, pre_update, fixed_update, update, post_update, transform, late_update) + after/before by system name; ties broken by order in world_desc.systems. Argument types never decide order, they only feed Debug access-conflict warnings
world_creation: one execution plan per world (ecs::build_system_plan), built when the world loads or its system list changes; contexts run in id order; data between contexts of a set goes through scn::set_channel (WORLD_MESSAGING.md)
modes: scn::context_set::set_mode(ecs::run_mode::edit|play|pause|step) — edit/pause run only run_in_edit systems

[IMGUI_PATTERNS]
begin_end_pairing:  # End() ALWAYS called; Begin() result only gates drawing
  if (ImGui::Begin("Panel")) {
    // render content
  }
  ImGui::End();
  # BeginChild/EndChild same; BeginPopup*/BeginMenu/BeginTable: End* only if Begin* returned true

layout:
  ImGui::Columns(N);
  ImGui::Separator();
  ImGui::Text("Label");
  ImGui::InputFloat("##id", &value);
  ImGui::NextColumn();

flags: Use ImGuiWindowFlags_*, ImGuiInputTextFlags_*, etc.

[GLM_PATTERNS]
precision: Default float (vec3, vec4, mat4)
includes: Only what you need (#include <glm/vec3.hpp>)
serialization: Use scn_glm_json_convert.h for descriptors
transformations: Apply matrices left-to-right (pos = M * pos)

[PERFORMANCE_PATTERNS]
no_statics_in_loops: Temporary data via frame_allocator
cache_locality: Structure of Arrays for systems processing components
early_exit: Return early to reduce branching
batch_operations: Group by resource type, render pass, etc.

[TESTING_PATTERNS]
framework: Boost.Test (BOOST_AUTO_TEST_SUITE, BOOST_AUTO_TEST_CASE)
location: tests/ directory
naming: SuffixTests or SuffixTest for suite, TestCaseName for cases
discovery: Auto via file(GLOB) in CMakeLists.txt
